---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nearby Towns & Cities | The Bluffs — Overlooking Weiss Lake"
  description="The Bluffs is ideally located near Rome GA, Fort Payne, Gadsden, and within 90 miles of Atlanta, Birmingham, and Chattanooga."
>

  <!-- PAGE HEADER -->
  <section class="section-sm page-header">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center">
      <h1>Nearby Towns and Cities</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        Perfectly situated in the heart of the ABC Triangle — roughly 90 miles from Atlanta,
        Birmingham, and Chattanooga — The Bluffs offers the peace of rural lake living without
        sacrificing access to major cities and amenities.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TOWNS CONTENT -->
  <section class="section-sm towns-section">
    <div class="container-narrow">

      <div class="town-entry">
        <h2>Cherokee County, Alabama</h2>
        <p>
          Home to The Bluffs, Cherokee County has a population of approximately 30,000 and
          is one of Alabama's 10 fastest-growing counties. Rich in Cherokee Native American
          and Civil War history, the county seat of Centre hosts a Cherokee heritage museum
          and a Civil War history museum, offering cultural depth alongside natural beauty.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="town-entry">
        <h2>Cedar Bluff, Alabama</h2>
        <p>
          The small town of Cedar Bluff (population approx. 1,500) sits at the gateway to
          The Bluffs community. Local businesses, grocery, and essential services are close
          at hand, while the town retains the quiet character that draws people to this
          corner of Alabama in the first place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="town-entry">
        <h2>Centre, Alabama</h2>
        <p>
          Centre is the Cherokee County seat, with a population of approximately 5,000. It
          offers a regional airport with a 9,000-foot runway capable of handling private and
          charter aircraft, a full-service hospital, and a growing selection of shopping and
          dining options — everything you'd expect from a well-established county hub.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <div class="town-entry">
        <h2>Rome, Georgia — 25 miles</h2>
        <p>
          A short 25-mile drive from The Bluffs, Rome, Georgia (population 35,000; metro
          approx. 90,000) is the closest significant city. Rome offers Harbin Clinic (a major
          regional medical center), minor league baseball, four colleges and universities,
          and a vibrant downtown district with restaurants and shops. It's the everyday
          city for many Bluffs residents.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="town-entry">
        <h2>Fort Payne, Alabama — 23 miles</h2>
        <p>
          Fort Payne is a 23-mile drive and serves as the gateway to some of the most
          scenic outdoor landscapes in the Southeast. The route via Little River Canyon
          National Preserve offers stunning gorge views, while DeSoto State Park provides
          hiking, waterfalls, and camping. Fort Payne itself (population 15,000) offers
          practical amenities along the way.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="town-entry">
        <h2>Gadsden, Alabama — 35 miles</h2>
        <p>
          Gadsden (population 40,000; metro over 100,000) is 35 miles from The Bluffs and
          offers big-city shopping, dining, medical facilities, and entertainment — including
          proximity to Talladega Superspeedway, one of NASCAR's most iconic venues, just
          45 miles further south.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <div class="town-entry abc-entry">
        <h2>The ABC Triangle</h2>
        <p>
          The Bluffs sits near the center of the "ABC Triangle" — Atlanta, Birmingham, and
          Chattanooga — making it one of the most accessible lake-and-mountain retreats in
          the Southeast for residents of any of those three metro areas.
        </p>
        <div class="abc-grid">
          <div class="abc-city">
            <h3>Atlanta, Georgia</h3>
            <p class="abc-distance">~90 miles</p>
            <p>
              Route: I-75 North to Hwy 411 through Rome, GA. Metro population 5.4 million.
              Hartsfield-Jackson International Airport provides worldwide connectivity for
              The Bluffs owners traveling internationally.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="abc-city">
            <h3>Birmingham, Alabama</h3>
            <p class="abc-distance">~90 miles</p>
            <p>
              Route: I-59 North to Gadsden. Metro population 1.2 million. Alabama's largest
              city offers a major medical district, university presence, and a full range of
              urban amenities within a 90-minute drive.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="abc-city">
            <h3>Chattanooga, Tennessee</h3>
            <p class="abc-distance">~80 miles</p>
            <p>
              Route: I-59 South to Fort Payne. Metro population approximately 500,000.
              Chattanooga is known for its revitalized riverfront, outdoor recreation culture,
              and as a hub for the growing Tennessee Valley tech and outdoor industries.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section-sm cta-band">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <p>Interested in visiting The Bluffs?</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/visit"   class="btn btn-primary">Get Directions</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-outline">Contact Us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-olive-light);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-intro {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .towns-section {
    padding-top: var(--space-12);
  }

  .town-entry {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .town-entry h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .town-entry p {
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  /* ABC Triangle */
  .abc-entry h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .abc-entry > p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .abc-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .abc-city {
    background: var(--color-cream-dark);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-olive);
  }

  .abc-city h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .abc-distance {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-olive);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .abc-city p:last-child {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* CTA band */
  .cta-band {
    background: var(--color-cream-dark);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-olive-light);
  }

  .cta-band p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .abc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
